From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:47:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] =?UTF-8?q?x86-64:=20port=20the=20i686=20code-bloat=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?fixes=20=E2=80=94=20never-materialized=20preview,=20escape-awar?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20DSE,=20post-inc=20spill=20forwarding?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports every applicable win from the i686 32K-boot-code campaign to the
x86-64 backend (the direct-to-dest ALU and slot-RMW folds already
existed there; the accumulator-bypass work originated as an x86-64
port to i686):

1. never_materialized fold preview (prologue): foldable GlobalAddr
   values (all uses become sym(%rip) accesses) are excluded from
   register allocation and slot assignment via
   run_regalloc_and_merge_clobbers_ex, with an x86-64-specific
   refinement dropping GOT-needing symbols (those DO materialize).
   Byte-identical output on the current benchmark corpus (registers
   are plentiful); pays off under pressure, and keeps the two
   backends' allocator contracts identical.

2. eliminate_never_read_stores: two unsound-bail relaxations, both
   with explicit proof obligations:
   * epilogue addq/pop/ret chains no longer disable the pass for
     every frame-pointer-less function (the shift is only followed by
     pops of below-frame slots and the terminator);
   * blanket indirect-access bail replaced by ESCAPE analysis - frame
     slots are only observable through leaq-of-slot or raw %rsp/%rbp
     value copies; without an escape event, pointer derefs cannot
     alias the fresh frame (C pointer args point at caller memory).
     Any escape still bails for the whole function.

3. combined_local_pass: store/reload forwarding across the stored
   register's own modifier (the post-inc/dec volatile-spill shape
   'movq %S,SLOT; leaq 1(%S),%S; movq SLOT,%D' -> hoisted
   'movq %S,%D' before the modifier). leaq is recognized as address
   arithmetic, not memory access. Combined with (2), the canonical
   *p++ byte loop drops its two per-iteration stack round-trips:
   loop body now matches GCC shape (movq %r11,%rdi; leaq 1(%r11)...).

Validation: 802/802 unit, 50/50 correctness, i686 regparm ABI green,
postinc runtime test green, hash_table asm byte-identical (timing
spread on the shared VM is noise), benchmark corpus size neutral
(25704 -> 25711 of gcc's 25813; the forwarding pattern trades one
5-byte store for a 3-byte reg move inside loops).
