MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

call TARGET; <pure epilogue>; ret  ->  <epilogue>; jmp TARGET
with i686 soundness rules:
* whole-function suppression on frame-address escape (leal of an
  %esp/%ebp slot) or dynamic alloca (subl %reg,%esp) — the callee
  could receive a pointer into the released frame (exactly why the
  bioscall-heavy boot files correctly do NOT convert);
* epilogue restores must not touch %eax/%edx (return value pair);
* plain  only (ret $N sret/fastcall cleanup differs);
* indirect call *%reg converts only when %reg is not restored by the
  epilogue between call and jmp.

Three unit tests pin the convert, the escape suppression, and the
restored-pointer rejection. 806/806 unit, 50/50 correctness, ABI
suites green; realmode corpus stable (its call sites pass local
addresses — suppression is the correct outcome there); wins accrue
to helper-call-heavy code (probe/dispatch shapes now match GCC).
